# Suave admin

Before editing the custom admin panel, RBAC, or admin conversation review:

1. **Read and follow** `.cursor/skills/suave-admin/SKILL.md`
2. Keep first-party roles/permissions — do not add Filament, Breeze, or Spatie Permission
3. Gate routes with `admin` + `permission:{name}`; gate nav with `hasPermission`
4. Put CRUD / domain logic in `App\Services\*Service`; keep Admin controllers thin (HTTP + flash/JSON only)
5. Put validation in `App\Http\Requests\Admin\*` Form Requests named `{Resource}StoreRequest` / `{Resource}UpdateRequest` (e.g. `BlogStoreRequest`) — no `$request->validate()` in controllers or services
6. Admin create/edit forms are **full width** by default — do not constrain with `max-width` unless the user asks
7. Before building create/edit/mutation UI, **ask the user** whether they want a **page** or a **modal** (unless already specified). Testimonials use index modals.
8. AI transcripts use Laravel AI SDK conversation tables via `ChatLead` — do not invent a parallel messages schema
9. Trend blog drafts: `blogs:generate-trend-drafts` + Tue/Fri schedule in `routes/console.php` (always `draft`; see suave-admin skill). Edit-form “Generate SEO meta” fills meta/OG inputs only — editor must save
10. UI: white admin theme (`#7539FF` primary, light sidebar) + Toastr/DataTables/Flatpickr/RichTextEditor; keep editor assets in `public/richtexteditor/`
11. Flash / toast feedback: PHP `createFlashMessage('Blog')` / `createFlashMessage('Blog', 'updated')` → "{Resource} has been {action} successfully." (always session `status`; no flash key from callers). Prefer `adminSuccess($request, 'Blog', 'created'|…)`. JS uses `SuaveAdmin.createFlashMessage(type, message)` with the server message. Do not call `toastr.*` or `Session::flash('status', …)` in new success paths
12. Contact inbox: `contacts.view` + `ContactRequest` — public form spam guards are honeypot/timing/throttle only (no third-party captcha); public store uses `ContactStoreRequest`
13. Roles UI: Admin → Roles (`roles.view` / `roles.manage`); protect the `admin` role key from rename/delete via `RoleService`
14. Testimonials: Admin → Testimonials (`testimonials.view` / `testimonials.manage`); create/edit via modal on index; frontend reads `TestimonialService::cachedForFrontend()` (forever cache, forget on write)
15. Marketing frontend / SuaveAgent widget work belongs under `suave-frontend`
